: West Virginia Aims for Second Consecutive Win, Faces TCU at Noon</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/24/football-game-day-west-virginia-aims-for-second-consecutive-win-faces-tcu-at-noon</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/24/football-game-day-west-virginia-aims-for-second-consecutive-win-faces-tcu-at-noon</guid><category>Football</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Running back Amari Latimer (1) scores a rushing touchdown in the fourth quarter against Cincinnati at Milan Puskar Stadium on Oct. 17, 2026." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/17/925314185-_dsc1338.jpg" /><br /><br />FORT WORTH, TEXAS — The West Virginia Mountaineers battle the TCU Horned Frogs at Amon G. Carter Stadium in Fort Worth, Texas, on Saturday at noon.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/17/925314185-_dsc1338.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/17/925314185-_dsc1338.jpg"><media:title>Running back Amari Latimer (1) scores a rushing touchdown in the fourth quarter against Cincinnati at Milan Puskar Stadium on Oct. 17, 2026.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/17/925314185-_dsc1338.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sat, 24 Oct 2026 07:45:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>2</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59578</s:story_id></item><item><title>Countdown to Kickoff: Mountaineers, Horned Frogs Tangle Today in Fort Worth</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/24/football-countdown-to-kickoff-mountaineers-horned-frogs-tangle-today-in-fort-worth</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/24/football-countdown-to-kickoff-mountaineers-horned-frogs-tangle-today-in-fort-worth</guid><category>Football</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Amon G. Carter Stadium" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2021/10/22/Amon_Stadium.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The popular expression "an unstoppable force meeting an immovable object" certainly applies to today's West Virginia-TCU football game being played at Amon G. Carter Stadium in Fort Worth, Texas.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2021/10/22/Amon_Stadium.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2021/10/22/Amon_Stadium.jpg"><media:title>Amon G. Carter Stadium</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2021/10/22/Amon_Stadium.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sat, 24 Oct 2026 07:00:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>2</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59577</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers Secure Win Over Arizona in Record-Breaking Performance</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/23/volleyball-mountaineers-secure-win-over-arizona-in-record-breaking-performance</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/23/volleyball-mountaineers-secure-win-over-arizona-in-record-breaking-performance</guid><category>Volleyball</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="WVU Volleyball celebrates as they defeat Arizona on Oct. 23" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/23/VB_vs.AZ_10.23_LH-06314.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. - The West Virginia University volleyball team (11-8, 4-5 Big 12) defeated Arizona, 3-1, on Friday evening at Hope Coliseum, earning its fourth Big 12 victory of the season by set scores of 23-25, 25-15,